  "mechanismSummary": "Cerium(III) chloride binds the carbonyl oxygen of cyclohex-2-enone, and borohydride (in methanol, partly as methoxyborohydrides) delivers hydride to the carbonyl carbon: 1,2-addition. Methanol protonates the oxygen as it leaves cerium, giving cyclohex-2-en-1-ol. Without CeCl₃, NaBH₄ gives a mixture with the 1,4-product, cyclohexanol after full reduction.",
